{
 "_doc": "Minecraft-style particles (ADR 0026). Units are metres and seconds. sprites: 8x8 pixel art, '.' clear, 1-9 grey level (tinted by the effect colour), letters from the sprite's palette (drawn as is); frames play over the particle's life. motions: gravity (m/s^2, down positive), drag (1/s), floor (rest | die | none), glow (emission), size_end (size at the end of life, times the start), sway (side drift, m/s). effects: channel chips (a random 4x4 pixel square of the block's atlas tile, like Minecraft's breaking particles) or sprites; count [min,max] (per_m / per_ms add per metre fallen / per m/s of speed, max caps), life [min,max] s, size [min,max] m, speed [min,max] m/s along dir (up | down | out | out_flat | face | any) within spread degrees, lift adds upward m/s, box half extents m, colors random pick, tint tile = the material's tile colour, shade random brightness. ambient: Minecraft's animateTick: cells sampled at random near the player spawn the effect with chance; where = any | air_above | air_below | water_above | furnace_front.",
